    "created_at": "2017-02-01T17:44:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-01T17:44:29Z",
    "body": "I'm concerned that this makes being same-origin dependent on the current value of `document.domain`. With the current definition, being same-origin is only dependent on the immutable data in an origin, this change would make it dependent on the mutable domain. (This is particularly problematic for cases where the same-origin check is being done in a different process, as it requires messaging.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
