    "created_at": "2017-02-01T18:08:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-01T18:08:16Z",
    "body": "The whole point of \"same origin\" as defined at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#same-origin is to be something that doesn't depend on document.domain at all.\r\n\r\nOK, let's look at where this definition is actually used in the spec, and assume the Chrome behavior is as described above:\r\n\r\n1. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#downloading-resources:same-origin -- this is comparing to a URL, so would always test false in Chrome for things that set document.domain.  Does it?\r\n2. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hyperlink-auditing:same-origin -- same thing.\r\n3. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#link-type-stylesheet:same-origin -- same thing.  Does Chrome forbid non-text/css stylesheets entirely on documents that have set document.domain?\r\n4. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#autofocusing-a-form-control:-the-autofocus-attribute:same-origin -- what does Chrome do here?\r\n5. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:same-origin -- not sure anyone implements any part of this requirement at all; I think there is an existing issue on that.\r\n6. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#security-nav:same-origin-2 -- what does Chrome actually do here?\r\n7. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#named-access-on-the-window-object:same-origin -- likewise?\r\n8. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-history-interface:same-origin -- does Chrome entirely disallow pushState/replaceState in documents that set document.domain?\r\n9. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigating-across-documents:same-origin -- does Chrome's javascript: handling enforce that the domain matches?\r\n10. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigating-across-documents:same-origin-5 -- does Chrome disallow about:blank reuse entirely for documents that have set document.domain?\r\n11. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#history-traversal:same-origin -- is the described behavior for browser context names something Chrome does?\r\n12. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#posting-messages:same-origin -- Does Chrome entirely prohibit posting messages to a window that has set document.domain?\r\n13. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#broadcasting-to-other-browsing-contexts:same-origin -- Does Chrome forbid broadcasting across different document.domain values?\r\n14. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#shared-workers-and-the-sharedworker-interface:same-origin-2 -- Does Chrome allow sharing SharedWorkers across document.domain differences?\r\n15. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#determining-the-character-encoding:same-origin -- does Chrome ignore the parent's character encoding for all subframes of a document that has set document.domain?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
